AquaStream360 DataMaster - User Guide

Overview
DataMaster is a data analysis and manipulation application  designed to handle very large datasets efficiently. It is particularly suited for users working with water-related data, including network data, simulation outputs, weather datasets, or water consumption records.
The application is built to simplify complex data workflows, offering tools to load, clean, analyze, and visualize data in an intuitive, user-friendly environment.
Main Interface Components
1. Top Toolbar (File Operations & Core Functions)
Located at the very top of the application, this section contains essential file operations and data management tools. A few of the available operations and buttons are explained below:
File Operations:
•	Import Data: Load data from Excel/CSV files
•	From PostgreSQL: Import data directly from PostgreSQL databases
•	Export Output Data: Save processed data to various formats
•	Export to Excel: Save data specifically as Excel files
•	Load Previous: Restore previously worked-on data
•	Example Data: Load sample datasets to explore features
Data Processing Tools:
•	Quick Scan: Generate a quick overview of your data
•	Visual Analysis: Create automatic visualizations
•	Auto Insights: Get intelligent data insights
•	Advanced Filter: Apply complex filtering rules
•	Manipulate: Access data transformation tools
•	Search: Find specific values across all data
•	Delete Row/Column: Remove rows or columns
•	Fill Missing Numbers/Texts: Handle empty values
•	Health Check: Assess data quality
•	Full Report: Generate comprehensive data reports
•	Box Plot: Create box plot visualizations
•	Group Detection: Automatically identify data groups
•	Append: Add new data to existing dataset
•	Heatmap: Create correlation heatmaps
•	Group By and Apply: Apply functions to grouped data
