3. Data Display Area
The central workspace showing your data:
Left Panel - INPUT DATA
•	Displays your original/imported data
•	Shows sheet names when working with Excel files
•	Hide Original Data: Toggle visibility of original dataset
•	Expand: Maximize workspace by hiding top toolbar
Right Panel - OUTPUT DATA
•	Shows results of your operations
•	Displays filtered, transformed, or analyzed data
•	Updates dynamically as you apply operations
Data Table Controls:
•	Set Index: Designate a column as row identifiers
•	Significant Figures: Control number precision
•	Editing Mode: Enable direct cell editing
•	Reset After Each Operation: Toggle between cumulative and step-by-step processing
•	Alternating Colors: Improve readability with striped rows
•	Undo/Redo: Reverse or reapply actions
•	Clear: Remove all data
•	Set As Original: Save current state as new baseline
•	Reset: Revert to original data
•	To Postgres: Export to PostgreSQL database
4. Editing Controls Panel
When Editing Mode is enabled, additional controls appear:
•	Reset: Undo all manual edits
•	Undo/Redo: Step through edit history
•	Export Data: Save edited dataset
•	Add/Remove Rows/Columns: Modify data structure
•	Rename Rows/Columns: Change labels
•	Show: Display data in original format
